    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft, Truesight 20 ft",
    "tactics": "Imps avoid combat. They spy, report, and sting when they have an overwhelming advantage. A Summoner who treats an Imp like a combat asset will be disappointed; one who treats it like an intelligence resource will get more than expected, though the information will always have a slight self-serving editorial slant.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Sting [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 2), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 5 damage (3 + 2 Str) + Fortitude [Easy] save or Poisoned (Weak) for 1 minute.</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 5 damage, DR halved (round up) + Fortitude [Easy] save or Poisoned (Strong) for 1 minute.</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Invisibility (At-Will): Imp can become invisible as a [Minor] action. Ends if it ### Attacks. Change Shape: Can assume the form of a small beast (rat, raven, spider) as a [Interact] action. Devil's Sight: Sees through magical darkness. Pocket Fiend: Imps are frequently used as spies and familiars by casters of dark intent. A Cooperative Imp will gather information reliably, though it exaggerates its own contribution significantly when reporting back.</p>",
